#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screen Reader"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:545
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Install a screen reader application like <ulink url=\"https://en.wikipedia."
"org/wiki/Orca_(assistive_technology)\">Orca</ulink> together with "
"<application>speech-dispatcher</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Test that sound from speech dispatcher works using the command <command>spd-"
"say hello</command> in a terminal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:554
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition you need a text to speech synthesizer like &eg; "
"<application>espeak</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enable the screen reader in the checkbox, logout and restart your desktop "
"session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For &plasma; itself, make sure to use the traditional <guilabel>Application "
"Menu</guilabel>, and check that this menu has a keyboard shortcut associated "
"(<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>F1</keycap></keycombo>). When "
"pressing this shortcut, the menu should open and be read when navigating the "
"menu with the arrow keys."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:569
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color Blindness Correction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is an accessibility tool designed to help users with color vision "
"deficiencies better distinguish between colors on their screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unlike simple filters that change the <quote>look</quote> of the desktop, "
"this feature uses <ulink url=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Color_blindness"
"\">daltonization algorithms</ulink>. These algorithms shift problematic "
"color frequencies into parts of the spectrum that the user can see more "
"clearly, helping to restore contrast that would otherwise be lost."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:577
#, no-c-format
msgid "Main objectives:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:582
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many interfaces use color to convey meaning (&eg;, green for <quote>success</"
"quote> and red for <quote>error</quote>). For someone with protanopia or "
"deuteranopia, these may look identical. The correction pane shifts these "
"colors so the distinction becomes visible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:587
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It ensures that buttons, graphs, and highlighted text are legible, "
"regardless of the original design's color palette."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:592
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Because it is handled at the compositor level (&kwin;), the correction "
"applies to everything—web browsers, specialized engineering software, "
"videos, and the desktop interface itself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The pane typically offers adjustments for the three primary types of color "
"blindness:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:602
#, no-c-format
msgid "Protanopia: Red-blindness (difficulty seeing red light)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:607
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deuteranopia: Green-blindness (the most common form)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:612
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tritanopia: Blue-blindness (rarer, difficulty distinguishing blue and "
"yellow)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Problematic colors</guilabel> selection: You select the "
"specific type of deficiency."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Intensity</guilabel> slider: This is the most important part "
"of the pane. It allows you to adjust the strength of the shift. Since color "
"vision is a spectrum, a \"one size fits all\" filter rarely works; the "
"slider lets you fine-tune the correction to your specific vision."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:624
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These filters are intended for accessibility, not for color-accurate work "
"like professional photo editing or digital painting. Because they shift the "
"color spectrum to make it \"readable,\" the colors on the screen will no "
"longer match the \"true\" hex codes or print values of the files you are "
"viewing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:628
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can control the results using <guilabel>Adjusted colors</guilabel> "
"swatches."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:634
#, no-c-format
msgid "Invert"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This pane configures a tool to flip the color values of your screen—turning "
"white pixels to black, blues to oranges, and so on. This is handled by the "
"&kwin; window manager as a post-processing effect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While it might look like a <quote>Negative</quote> photo filter, its primary "
"purposes are functional rather than aesthetic:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For users with specific visual impairments, such as photophobia (light "
"sensitivity) or certain types of low vision, a standard bright screen can "
"cause physical pain or make text appear blurry due to <quote>light bleed.</"
"quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:645
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Inverting the screen turns bright backgrounds dark and dark text light, "
"significantly reducing the amount of light emitted by the monitor while "
"maintaining the contrast needed to read."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:648
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While most modern applications have native dark modes, some older software "
"or specific web pages are hard-coded with white backgrounds."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:651
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Invert tool acts as a <quote>universal dark mode.</quote> If an "
"application doesn't support a dark theme, you can force the colors to invert "
"to save your eyes during late-night work sessions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:654
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can switch on the inversion using the <guilabel>Invert</guilabel> "
"checkbox and <guibutton>Configure Shortcuts...</guibutton> for this action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:660
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shake Pointer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:662
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the &plasma; desktop environment, the <guilabel>Shake Pointer</guilabel> "
"(often colloquially called \"Shake to Find\") is an accessibility and "
"productivity feature designed to solve the \"lost cursor\" problem."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:665
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are using a multi-monitor setup, an ultra-high-resolution display, or "
"simply have a dark wallpaper, it is remarkably easy to lose track of where "
"the mouse cursor is. The purpose of this feature is to provide an immediate "
"visual clue to help you locate it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:668
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the feature is enabled, the system monitors the velocity and direction "
"of mouse movements. If it detects a rapid back-and-forth \"shaking\" motion:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:673
#, no-c-format
msgid "Temporary enlargement: The cursor increases in size to the large scale."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:678
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Visual focus: This sudden change in scale catches the human eye’s peripheral "
"vision, instantly revealing the cursor's coordinates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:683
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Automatic reset: As soon as you stop shaking the mouse, the cursor shrinks "
"back to its normal size."
msgstr ""

